USEFUL CHECKS
==================================================

Where am I?
pwd

What files are here?
ls

Is Git installed?
git --version

What changed?
git status

What GitHub repo is connected?
git remote -v

What commits exist?
git log --oneline

What branch am I on?
git branch


==================================================
IMPORTANT RULES
==================================================

1. One main project = one Git repository.

2. Don't run git init inside every subfolder.

3. Don't upload virtual environments.

4. Always check git status before committing.

5. Don't blindly use:
   rm -rf

6. Commit messages should describe what changed.

7. You normally DON'T need:
   git init
   git remote add origin
   git branch -M main

   every time.

   Those are mainly FIRST-TIME setup commands.


==================================================
THE 4 COMMANDS YOU WILL USE MOST
==================================================

git status
git add .
git commit -m "What I changed"
git push


